      "run": 0,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I found myself standing in a cramped, salty galley where the mist of the sea seemed to have permeated everything. With a kettle tucked under my arm, a remnant of what was likely an abandoned hope for a warm drink, I navigated through the narrow confines to the north, emerging into what was once a storeroom. The scent of paraffin clung to the stale air, and the sight of empty shelves spoke volumes about the passage of time and the people who once filled this space with purpose. Taking a coil of rope, which seemed like it could be useful for any number of reasons, I felt the weight of potential tasks ahead.\n\nHeading back the way I came from this desolate storeroom, I pondered over the eerie quietness of the ship. It was a ghost of its former self; sails long since surrendered to the winds, the crew gone, leaving behind their utensils and tools. As I looked around, the kettle and rope felt like the only tangible connections to a time when this ship embarked on daring adventures across the treacherous oceans.",
